(b) shall remain present at concerned Police Station on 21 s t Ju n e, 20 24 .
(c) shall not directly or indirectly make any inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the fact of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the court or to any police officer;
(d) shall not obstruct or hamper the police investigation and not to play mischief with the evidence collected or yet to be collected by the police;
(e) shall at the time of execution of bond, furnish the address to the investigating officer and the court concerned and shall not change residence till the final disposal of the case till further orders;
(f) shall not leave India without the permission of the concerned trial court and if having passport shall deposit the same before the concerned NEUTRAL CITATION R/CR.MA/10402/2024 ORDER DATED: 11/06/2024 undefined trial court within a week;
(g) it would be open to the Investigating Officer to file an application for remand if he considers it proper and just and the learned Magistrate would decide the remand application without being influenced of the observations made by this Court; and (h) The applicant shall deposit the amount of Rs. 9 lakhs before the concerned trial court within a period of 3 weeks from the date of the order and shall file an undertaking to the said effect before the concerned trial court.

